Disable Bluedroid power-management sniff requests for the Classic BT HID
device (HD) profile.

By default Bluedroid's BTA DM PM layer issues HCI_Sniff_Mode on every
"busy" event (i.e. every HID report sent) with a 0 ms delay, and again
on "idle" and "conn open" after 5 s.  Linux accepts the sniff request;
the resulting Sniff→Active round-trip takes ~40–50 ms, which dominates
input latency.  Mac/Android reject the sniff request, so they don't
suffer the same penalty.

Zeroing the allowed-modes mask for the HD entry causes bta_dm_pm.c
(line ~565: pm_action = allowed_modes & (PARK|SNIFF) & pref_modes) to
evaluate to BTA_DM_PM_NO_ACTION for every event, so no sniff is ever
requested.

--- a/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/dm/bta_dm_cfg.c
+++ b/components/bt/host/bluedroid/bta/dm/bta_dm_cfg.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@

     /* HD : 6 */
     {
-        (BTA_DM_PM_SNIFF | BTA_DM_PM_PARK),                            /* allow park & sniff */
+        BTA_DM_PM_NO_ACTION,                                           /* sniff disabled: bridge needs low latency */
 #if (BTM_SSR_INCLUDED == TRUE)
         (BTA_DM_PM_SSR3),                                              /* the SSR entry */
 #endif
